  <div class="eye">RESEARCH · AI SECURITY ECONOMICS</div>
  <h1 class="page-title">Anthropic Frontier Red Team & Cyber Verification Program: The Economics of AI Security Testing</h1>
  <p class="updated">Security Economics Analysis · 21 October 2026</p>
  <p class="byline">By the LLM CFO team</p>

  <p class="lede">On October 20, 2026, Anthropic published research showing its Frontier Red Team using Opus 5.5 to automatically reduce attack surfaces across 25 open-source projects (5M+ lines of code), discovering 493 security issues. Days earlier, on October 6, they launched the three-tier Cyber Verification Program (CVP) that gates access to these same capabilities. This analysis covers what security teams need to budget, plan, and provision.</p>

  <h2>The Research: Attack Surface Reduction at Scale</h2>
  <p>Anthropic's Frontier Red Team applied three automated techniques to 25 projects (C, C++, Java, PHP, Python):</p>
