  <p><strong>Key insight:</strong> Red Team Access achieves the same 68% completion rate as running Opus 5.5 with <em>no safeguards at all</em>. The tier doesn't change model capability — it changes whether Anthropic's classifiers intervene.</p>

  <h3>What Each Tier Permits</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Defense Access:</strong> Secure code review, threat modeling, patching known issues, finding vulns in your own source, triaging alerts. Malware analysis and exploit validation will be blocked.</li>
    <li><strong>Red Team Access:</strong> All Defense activities + malware analysis, exploit validation, offensive scenario testing, red-team exercises. No classifier blocks on CyScenarioBench.</li>
    <li><strong>Specialized Access:</strong> Red Team capabilities + access to Mythos 5.1 (limited availability) + deepest model versions. Requires US government collaboration.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Enterprise Budget & Provisioning Implications</h2>

  <h3>1. Verification & Onboarding Costs</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Application review:</strong> ~7 business days for decision.</li>
    <li><strong>MFA migration:</strong> Defense Access requires phishing-resistant MFA by December 15, 2026. API keys expire every 7 days until migrated. Budget for Workload Identity Federation rollout.</li>
    <li><strong>Org admin overhead:</strong> Assigning programs to workspaces (Console), custom roles (Enterprise), or linked accounts (Bedrock/GCP/AWS/Azure).</li>
    <li><strong>Mythos provisioning:</strong> ~5 business days after approval, trails main CVP grant.</li>
  </ul>

