  <h2>Opt-In Vulnerability Finding Service (Launched Oct 8)</h2>
  <p>Anthropic also launched a free, opt-in vulnerability scanner for open-source projects, powered by their strongest models. Projects receive periodic security scans at no cost. This is a direct productization of the Frontier Red Team's research methodology. Enterprise teams should evaluate whether their open-source dependencies participate — it reduces the attack surface of your supply chain at zero cost.</p>

  <h2>Recommendations for Security & Finance Leaders</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Apply for CVP now if you do any offensive security testing.</strong> The 92% block rate on Defense Access makes it unusable for red-team workflows. Red Team Access is the only viable tier for malware analysis, exploit validation, and offensive scenario testing.</li>
    <li><strong>Budget for MFA migration by Dec 15, 2026.</strong> Phishing-resistant MFA (hardware keys, WebAuthn, Workload Identity Federation) is mandatory for Defense Access. API keys expire weekly until migrated.</li>
    <li><strong>Plan for Mythos 5.1 access lag.</strong> If you need Mythos, factor ~5 business days post-approval. Mythos follows Fable 5.1 usage rules on Pro/Max (usage credits required, shared 50% weekly allowance).</li>
    <li><strong>Track CVP grant as a security asset.</strong> Include CVP tier, expiration, and Mythos access status in your AI security posture dashboard. A lapsed grant = immediate reversion to 92% block rate.</li>
    <li><strong>Evaluate third-party tool CVP support.</strong> If your coding agents (Cursor, Copilot, etc.) don't support CVP enrollment links, your engineers lose Red Team capabilities in those tools.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Bottom Line for CFOs</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>AI security testing without CVP Red Team Access is economically non-viable.</strong> 92% block rate = 12.5× cost inflation per completed assessment.</li>
    <li><strong>CVP is a security budget line item, not an AI budget line item.</strong> It enables the security team to use AI tools they already pay for (Opus 5.5 API).</li>
    <li><strong>MFA migration is the hidden CapEx.</strong> Phishing-resistant MFA rollout across the org is a prerequisite, not an option.</li>
    <li><strong>Supply chain benefit is free.</strong> The opt-in vulnerability scanner for open-source dependencies reduces your attack surface at zero cost — ensure your key dependencies enroll.</li>
  </ul>